  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In Build 1547, a small bug was fixed that caused the user status to overlap with the trust rank on a user's profile. While this fix addresses the issue by truncating the user status, further adjustments are recommended.\n\nOne notable issue is the excessive padding at the bottom of the user element. This padding was introduced when the element was adjusted downward to accommodate the addition of tabs at the top of the profile in Build 1546. However, the user status and trust rank text do not appear to account for this adjustment.\n\nThis problem also affects profiles beyond the user's own where the tabs are not visible. Adjusting the position of the trust rank downward to reduce some of the padding would be a preferable solution. This change would also eliminate the need for the user status to be truncated, as it should no longer overlap with the trust rank. This would be preferable as many might find truncation of their status to be undesirable. At the very least, truncation should only occur if someone somehow managed to make a status that occupies more then two lines.",
